From 5e5cc3c790de03dcfee32548a91bba861d194bac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 10:22:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Hades][AudioEngine] The outputs are not listed again after a
 reset of the display where only ELDs changed and came back as they were

Every video that started with a change of display mode on the owner's
RTX 4080 SUPER started without its sound: the audio stream was made
514 to 543 ms after the first try, came 453 to 495 ms behind the
video, and was put back with that much left out. The change of mode
clears the ELD of the HDMI output and sets it again with the same
bytes; ALSA tells both, the audio engine (suspended for the lost
display) kept "a device change came", and when the display was back it
listed every output of the PC again, which took 530 to 550 ms in which
no stream could be made ("the outputs changed while the display was
being reset: they are listed again").

CALSAHControlMonitor keeps the bytes of each ELD control as the listing
of the outputs reads it (Add()) and as each of its events leaves it,
and an ELD event tells the engine whether every ELD is as it was listed
(IAE::EldChange(); an engine that does not tell them apart takes it as
any device change). While suspended for a lost display, the engine
keeps that (ActiveAESuspendedChanges.h: the last ELD event stands for
all of them) apart from any other device change. When the display is
back it lists the outputs again where another device changed (a card,
a driver, the default device) or an ELD is not as it was listed
(another display, other audio data, one still away: the event that
brings it back is acted on as any other), and otherwise opens the
output again as it was, and kodi.log says so. In every other state an
ELD event is a device change event, as before.

The output that the user chose and the outputs kept lit for its sound
(issue #24, ActiveAEFollowDisplay.h, ActiveAEKeptOutputs.h) are decided
by a listing: with the ELDs as they were, the listing that decided them
is the one that stands, and it would read the same.
